## Iteration 6 — 2026-04-16

Mixed iteration — a legitimate framework bug fix, two polish-level
visual fixes, one code-cleanliness migration, and one meta-lesson
about the limits of the Gemini cross-check loop.

### What shipped

* **Button hover-outline bug** (same class as the iter-4 Panel-shadow
  bug): ``theme.button_hover_outline_color`` is opaque, so a ghost
  (alpha-0) button that the user intentionally styled as invisible
  would grow a visible blue glow on hover. Now the outline is
  skipped when the *explicit* style carries alpha-0 background.
  Two regression tests (transparent → 0 glow rects, opaque → ≥1).
  Audit of Tooltip + TabGroup draws came up clean; the bug was
  Panel + Button, both fixed.
* **Heart node is green** — ``+`` node background/rim went from
  pink (confusingly similar to enemy red) to green. Gain and threat
  now read as different categories of information at a glance. One
  line in the NODE_STYLES map; Gemini had flagged this every round
  since v8.
* **Sub-label placement is radial outward** — every node's info
  label pushes *away* from the ring centre rather than straight
  down, so the O-node's ``→ floor 2`` no longer bleeds into the
  E-node directly beneath it. Horizontal anchor chosen per-node
  from the radial direction so labels grow outward instead of back
  toward the ring.
* **Player pip flipped INSIDE the ring** — the pip and "YOU"
  caption used to fight sub-labels for the same outside-the-ring
  space. With radial sub-labels claiming *outside*, the player
  token now lives *inside* the ring, pointing outward at the
  current node. The two visual channels never collide again
  regardless of which node the player is on.
* **`handle_input` replaced by `bind_key`** — Ring of Pain's input
  went from a nested if-else on `event.action` / `event.key` to
  six flat `self.bind_key(...)` calls in a new `_bind_controls()`
  helper. The scene describes *what* each key does, not *how* the
  event dispatcher routes it.

Screenshot: ``/tmp/ring_of_pain_v12.png``. 164 tests pass (2 new
regression tests; 12 from iter 5 carried forward).

### Meta-lesson: Gemini oscillation as a structural ceiling

v10 Gemini asked for message *out* of the ring; v12 Gemini (now
that the centre is quieter) asks for it back *inside* because the
outside "feels chaotic." v9 Gemini called the white glow a
"selection inconsistency"; v10 called its absence a "weak player
indicator"; v12 called the radial sub-label layout — which fixed
a concrete collision — "chaotic text placement." The same model
flips on the same questions across rounds.

This is the ceiling of the single-LLM cross-check loop. Beyond
~v8, Gemini's feedback is *drift*, not signal. The right read is:

* **Before ~v8**: Gemini catches concrete, reproducible issues
  (title/node collision, ambiguous player marker, casing,
  missing sub-labels). Take these seriously.
* **After ~v8**: Gemini ranks aesthetic preferences that oscillate
  each round. Any fix will satisfy one round and displease the
  next. Use Gemini's *agreement across rounds* (heart-pink
  called out in v8/v9/v10 → real) rather than any single round's
  recommendation.

Parked for beyond this exercise: cross-check against a *second*
independent model (GPT-5.x) and treat consensus between them as
signal; single-model drift is noise.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **`bind_key` doesn't support aliases directly.** Each raw-key
   alias (WASD + arrows, space + enter) needs its own call. A
   `bind_keys(["right", "d"], callback)` or list-keyed form would
   halve the boilerplate.
2. **`_lighten_color` is duplicated** four times across
   `ui/widgets.py` (ProgressBar, List, Tooltip, TabGroup). Not a
   bug; worth a `util` extraction when the file gets its next
   edit.
3. **Theme has opaque colour constants that stay visible against
   user intent**. The Panel-shadow and Button-hover-outline bugs
   share root cause: a theme property draws when the component
   says "I'm invisible." A `Theme.is_decoration_enabled(component)`
   hook — or a blanket rule that alpha-0 components skip every
   decoration — would close the class. Flagged for future.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

One legitimate framework bug fixed (Button hover outline on
transparent). Three UX improvements (heart colour, radial
sub-labels, pip inside ring). One code-cleanliness migration
(handle_input → bind_key). One meta-lesson logged.

### Parked for iteration 7

* **`bind_keys([...], cb)` list form** — cut the alias boilerplate.
* **Bundle a game font** — the single biggest remaining visual
  complaint from every Gemini round.
* **Cross-check with a second model (GPT-5.x)** — treat consensus
  as signal, single-model drift as noise.
* **Message out of ring centre**: YOU pip now lives inside; a
  large message there fights it when the player is at the top
  node. Move to ``Anchor.TOP`` below title.
* **`_lighten_color` deduplication** into a util module.

