## Iteration 9 — 2026-04-16

This is the first iteration whose plan was *dictated by the auto-
consensus synthesiser* from iter-8 rather than by single-model critique
or my own aesthetic judgment. Three consensus items shipped, plus the
``_lighten_color`` dedup.

### What shipped

* **Acted on iter-8 synthesis recommendation**: uniform node-label
  placement. All sub-labels now sit at a fixed vertical offset
  below their node, centred, same font style. Reverts iter-6's
  radial layout because two independent reviewers agreed the
  radial placement read as "chaotic."
* **Sub-label copy tightened** to fit the below-node footprint
  without horizontal collisions::

      enemy    → "3 HP · 1 ATK"      (was "3 HP  1 atk")
      treasure → "+5 GOLD"           (was "+5g")
      heart    → "+3 HP"             (unchanged)
      shop     → "SHOP"              (was "shop")
      portal   → "FLOOR 2"           (was "→ floor 2")

  Dropping the ``→`` arrow character removed the iter-3-era
  collision between the portal label and the adjacent enemy node.
* **Player pip moved to always-above-node**. With sub-labels now
  uniformly below, placing the YOU pip uniformly above guarantees
  the two visual channels never share pixels — regardless of
  which node the player is on. For the top node the pip sits
  outside the ring; for the bottom node, inside. The rule is one
  line of code.
* **Default theme font** changed from ``"serif"`` to
  ``"Avenir Next Condensed"``. macOS system face, zero-asset
  change, visibly more polished than the previous rendering.
  Every cross-check round has flagged typography; this is the
  first response that actually lands in pixels.
* **``saga2d.util.color.lighten(color, factor)``** extracted from
  four identical ``_lighten_color`` methods (ProgressBar, List,
  Tooltip, TabGroup). All four call sites now call the shared
  helper directly. Five property tests cover identity, clamping,
  alpha preservation, darkening, zero-factor safety. **Per
  CLAUDE.md rule 6 ("don't deprecate, delete"), the local shim
  methods were removed outright rather than kept as aliases.**
* **Ring geometry nudged 0.33 → 0.32** so the bottom-node
  sub-label clears the status message above the HUD without
  making side-node labels touch the adjacent discs.

Screenshot: ``/tmp/ring_of_pain_v19.png``. 566 tests pass.

### Meta: first synthesis-driven iteration

Iter-8 shipped the auto-consensus machinery. This round proved it
actually reduces cycle time. The v15 synthesis output::

    ## RECOMMENDED NEXT ACTION
    Define and apply a consistent text positioning system: place all
    node labels at a fixed vertical offset below their circles,
    centred.

…was the literal plan of iter-9's first task. No human had to read
the raw critiques and decide; the recommendation was already
extracted. Saves ~2 minutes of an iteration, which matters when
the wall clock is 5.

The v17/v19 cross-check still produced a synthesis — unsurprisingly,
it now flags "message crowds bottom enemy subtext" (both models)
rather than radial placement, because that specific issue was fixed.
The method is working: each round the consensus recommendation
points at the *next* most actionable item, not the same one.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Cross-check loop is hitting a content floor** — reviewers
   keep reaching for typography + hierarchy. Both a bundled
   distinctive font and stricter line-height-ish rules in the
   default theme would raise the floor. Not this iteration.
2. **Iterating on ring-layout geometry is trial-and-error**.
   There's no helper that says "given a viewport size and a
   ring count, what's the max ring_r that keeps labels from
   colliding?" A ``layout_budget(viewport, nodes, label_w)``
   utility could make this a one-liner. Flagged for when more
   than one saga2d game needs rings.
3. **Ring layouts always read as "chaotic" to vision LLMs**
   compared to rectangular lists — likely a training-data bias
   toward grid UIs. Worth noting so future iterations don't
   chase consensus feedback that is actually model bias.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

Three consensus-driven visual fixes (unified label placement,
pip-always-above, better font) plus one dedup (``lighten``). The
first iteration planned from the auto-synthesiser's output rather
than from single-model reviews.

### Parked for iteration 10

* **Bundle a custom game font**. System fonts (Avenir) took the
  edge off but "typography feels generic" may keep surfacing.
  Permissive-licence display face (e.g. ``Cinzel``, ``IM FELL``)
  vendored under ``assets/fonts/``.
* **Synthesis fallback when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY absent** — naive
  string-overlap of the two critiques when no Claude key is
  configured.
* **``ReactiveValue.default`` ergonomic simplification**.
* **``layout_budget`` utility** for radial-layout sizing given
  viewport + label widths.
* **Auto-run cross-check + synthesis as part of ``screenshot.py``**
  so the one-liner ``./screenshot.py`` produces the synthesis
  write-up automatically, not as a separate command.

