  mock-backend is excellent at.

699 mock-backend tests pass.

### Why the non-radial example matters more than a radial one

After 12 iterations of saga2d development driven by Ring of Pain,
and one iteration (13) generalising to another radial game
(dial menu), there was a real risk the framework had quietly
specialised on rings. The tic-tac-toe example is the strongest
possible disproof: different layout primitive (``grid_positions``),
different input shape (clamped grid navigation, not wrap-around),
different game loop (turn-based with win state, not continuous
rotation), different HUD shape (top-centre + bottom-centre, not
corners).

Everything it needed already existed. No new framework code
beyond this one example file and its tests. The iter-2..14 stack
generalises to both radial *and* grid-based games from the same
primitives — which is what "Keras for game dev" has always meant
in these logs: describe the game, not the engine.

