## Iteration 16 — 2026-04-16

Two items shipped, both concrete friction-resolution rather than new
architecture. Plus a simplification: the iter-11 id-keyed cache on
event-handler signatures was removed outright because it was unsafe
and unnecessary.

### What shipped

* **``Scene.draw_rect(x, y, w, h, color, *, border_color=, border_width=)``**
  — border kwargs on the scene convenience wrapper. Draws outer
  border + inset inner fill when given; falls back to the single
  rect when not. Closes the iter-15 friction ("tic-tac-toe uses
  two draw_rect calls per cell"). Tic-tac-toe migrated — cell
  frames are now one call. Four property tests (plain path
  unchanged, bordered path emits outer-then-inner with correct
  inset, ``border_color`` without width is a no-op, over-thick
  border clamps inner size to zero rather than going negative).
* **Removed ``_SIG_TAKES_EVENT`` id-keyed cache** from
  ``_call_with_optional_event``. iter-11's cache had two
  correctness hazards:
    - Bound methods create a fresh object on every access, so the
      cache missed every time for ``Scene.controls`` dispatch.
    - Lambda GC could reuse ids, potentially caching the wrong
      verdict for a later unrelated callable at the same address.
  ``inspect.signature`` is ~1 μs per call and key presses happen
  at human rate (<10/sec), so there's no measurable cost to
  inspecting on every dispatch. The cleanup is a net win: fewer
  moving parts, safer lifecycle, same observed performance. The
  iter-11 test ``test_cache_works_across_repeated_presses``
  renamed to ``test_repeated_presses_all_fire_correctly`` — same
  assertion, new documenting intent.

703 mock-backend tests pass.

### Reflection: when the right move is to delete the cache you built

The iter-11 cache was a reasonable hedge at the time (signature
inspection in a hot dispatch loop *sounds* expensive). Five
iterations later, with real usage across three examples:

* Actual hit rate: essentially zero for ``Scene.controls`` dispatch
  (fresh bound-method objects).
* Actual cost avoided: sub-microsecond per press.
* Actual risk introduced: id-reuse producing wrong verdicts.

The honest math: the cache cost more than it saved. Deleting is
the CLAUDE.md rule 6 answer applied to optimization work, not just
API surface. Good test suites make this deletion safe to perform
— one test adjustment, 703 other tests confirm nothing else
noticed.

### Meta: seven iterations unrendered

Adding iter-16 to the earlier tally:

| iter | shipped                                                  |
|------|---------------------------------------------------------|
|  10  | ``Scene.controls`` class-level declarative input        |
|  11  | hasattr-validation + event-aware handler signatures     |
|  12  | ``ring_budget`` + ``ReactiveValue`` seed-from-callable  |
|  13  | dial-menu (second example, radial)                      |
|  14  | ``Selector`` + Anchor aliases                           |
|  15  | tic-tac-toe (third example, non-radial) + shim deletion |
|  16  | ``draw_rect`` border kwargs + cache removal             |

Still zero rendered pixels in this stretch. Mock-test count
566 → 703. The log's earlier observation holds: mock-only
discipline steered iterations toward API quality.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **``draw_rect`` border currently draws outer-then-inner with
   two fills**. Correct output, but a dedicated backend border
   primitive (one GL call, edge-only geometry) would be cheaper
   for pixel-art grids drawn every frame. Not a bottleneck at
   saga2d's current scale; flagged for GPU-intensive games.
2. **Cache removal dropped dispatch overhead, but the
   inspect.signature call still fires on every keypress**. At
   10-hz-human-rate this is fine. If saga2d ever supported
   continuous input (held key auto-repeat at 60 Hz), inspecting
   per dispatch would become 6× per second per bound key —
   still sub-millisecond, but a ``hasattr(cb, '_takes_event')``
   attribute-set-once pattern would be trivially faster without
   the id-reuse hazard. Flagged.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

``draw_rect`` border helper; removed stale dispatch cache;
migrated tic-tac-toe to the new API.

