Ten consecutive mock-only iterations. Mock-test count 566 → 723.
Every API surface change in this run has a test; the no-render
discipline has not cost correctness signal. The cost has been
zero visual polish in ten rounds — the bundled-game-font item
has now survived more iterations than any other parked item
(ten, as the tally shows).

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **``walk()`` yields all components including invisible ones**.
   An invisible subtree is still walked. For layout inspection
   this is what you want (invisible components still have
   computed rects). For drawing-related walks it isn't. A
   ``visible_only=True`` flag would help; not urgent.
2. **``find`` uses a predicate callable**. Nice and flexible,
   but a CSS-selector-like convenience (``find("Label[text^=HP]")``)
   is a real option later. Over-engineering for now; callables
   are fine.

