### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Tuple round-trip through JSON is a real trap**. The
   ``background_color`` field had to be converted to a list
   explicitly or ``json.dumps`` would coerce it to a list while
   the tuple form silently became a list on read. Choosing list-
   on-output makes the contract obvious.
2. **Reactive values deliberately omit their snapshot in
   ``summary_json``**. ``text: {"reactive": true}`` has no
   ``value`` key — the point is snapshot stability. A consumer
   that wants live values can always read the actual Label.
3. **``Anchor`` is serialised as its ``.name`` string** (e.g.
   ``"TOP_LEFT"``). That's the stable human-readable identifier
   even though ``TOP_LEFT`` and ``TOP_CENTER`` share the same
   underlying enum member (iter-14 aliases). If a consumer
   deserialises, it reads back to the original enum correctly.

