### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Three snapshot test files are near-identical**
   (three lines of imports, a fixture, one assertion). A tiny
   pytest plugin or fixture factory would collapse them. Not
   urgent — the duplication is ~15 lines per file.
2. **Bootstrapping a snapshot is silent**. The first test run
   writes the file without any stdout message, so a developer
   could miss that a snapshot was created when they didn't
   expect one. A one-line ``print`` on creation would help;
   parked, minor.
3. **``SAGA2D_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1`` is session-global**. If a
   single test in a large suite should accept its new snapshot
   while others should still assert, the developer has to
   filter with ``-k``. A per-snapshot ``force_update=True``
   kwarg would let tooling bypass the env-var for targeted
   updates. Parked.

