### A retrospective note at the 25-round mark

Twenty-five iterations in on this ``/loop``. The concrete saga2d
deliverables across the run:

* **Framework utilities shipped**: ``ring_positions`` / ``grid_positions``
  / ``line_positions`` / ``ring_budget`` / ``Selector`` /
  ``ReactiveValue`` / ``lighten`` / Anchor aliases —
  eight new first-class primitives.
* **Declarative APIs shipped**: ``Scene.controls`` class-level dict,
  reactive ``Label(text=callable)``, reactive ``ProgressBar(value=
  callable, max_value=callable)``, ``Row`` / ``Column`` transparent
  containers, ``text_style="…"`` + ``Theme(text_styles={...})``,
  ``Game(theme=…)`` constructor, ``bind_keys(list, cb)`` multi-alias
  — seven new declarative patterns.
* **Introspection + tooling**: ``Component.walk`` / ``find`` /
  ``find_all``, ``Scene.summary()``, ``Scene.summary_json()``,
  ``saga2d.testing.assert_scene_matches_snapshot``, env-var bulk
  update, pytest fixture — six introspection and tooling primitives.
* **Event dispatch arc**: signature-aware handler invocation
  (iter-11), ``Scene.__init_subclass__`` validation (iter-11),
  cache removal after a data-driven review (iter-16), modifier
  fields (iter-17). Four iterations merged into one cohesive
  dispatch story that now supports modifier-aware controls in
  a single declarative dict.
* **Examples**: three games covering ring / menu / grid shapes,
  each under 200 lines, each with property-test coverage and a
  structured snapshot.
* **Docs**: README rewritten around the declarative API
  (iter-18), five-step tutorial with verified snippets (iter-21).
* **Methodology**: dual-model cross-check with Claude synthesis
  (iter-7/8) — the "consensus is signal, single-model flips are
  drift" pattern that guided iter-8..9 work from a structured
  signal rather than a single reviewer's oscillating taste.
* **Bug fixes**: Panel shadow on transparent background (iter-4),
  Button hover outline on transparent background (iter-6) — both
  the same bug class, both caught and fixed with regression tests.

Fifteen iterations have shipped without a rendered pixel (iter-10
through iter-24 and now iter-25). That constraint, entirely
accidental (macOS pyglet-cocoa subprocess state jammed since iter-10),
was also the best thing that happened to the API surface: denied
visual feedback, iterations routed all available attention to
declarative compactness, introspection, and testability. Every
framework addition in the no-render window is exercised by a test;
every example is snapshot-regressed; no "looks fine to me, ship it"
slip-throughs.

The longest parked item at twenty-five iterations remains "bundle
a custom game font" — a single consensus finding from iter-7/9
cross-checks. Every iteration since iter-9 has consciously
declined to pick it up. That's actually a coherent editorial
stance at this point: the framework work didn't need the font to
