### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Font family name may differ from filename stem**. Cinzel's
   TTF has family metadata ``"CinzelRoman"`` (variable-weight
   format quirk). ``load_font(stem="Cinzel")`` registers the
   pyglet alias as "Cinzel" but whether that matches the
   internal family at render time is only verifiable with a
   working display. Flagged — might need a metadata-parsing
   step that uses the font's declared family name instead of
   the filename stem.
2. **``_register_bundled_fonts`` swallows all exceptions**.
   Defensive, but a "none of your fonts loaded" game would be
   silent. A logging hook or warning would help. Minor.
3. **Font registration is now a side effect of creating an
   AssetManager**. Games that construct an AssetManager for
   non-rendering reasons (unit tests, CI) still trigger the
   scan. Cost is low (directory listing + N load_font calls,
   all mock-backend no-ops in tests) but noted.

