## Iteration 28 — 2026-04-17

Closed a parked item that had been waiting since iter-20:
``summary(include_bounds=True)``. Completes the introspection
API's layout-debugging story — a developer hitting "why isn't this
Label where I expected" now has a one-line answer.

### What shipped

* **``Scene.summary_json(include_bounds=True)``** — each UI node
  gains ``"bounds": [x, y, w, h]`` from its computed rect.
* **``Scene.summary(include_bounds=True)``** — the formatted
  string gets a ``bounds=[x,y WxH]`` tag appended to each
  component's one-line description.
* **Default remains ``False``** — bounds depend on viewport size,
  so including them by default would make every snapshot test
  resolution-coupled. Off-by-default keeps
  ``assert_scene_matches_snapshot`` stable.
* **``_ui._ensure_layout()`` call** before reading bounds, so
  components added in ``on_enter`` that haven't yet laid out
  produce real coordinates rather than zeros.
* **7 property tests**: absent-by-default, present-when-requested
  (root has ``[0, 0, w, h]``), bounds propagate through
  containers, JSON-serialisable (round-trips through
  ``json.dumps``), formatted string has bounds-tag on every
  visible node when on, default formatted string has no bounds
  tag, **resolution-coupling check** (two games at different
  sizes produce different bounds — documenting the reason bounds
  default off).

795 mock-backend tests pass (7 new).

### Sample output with ``include_bounds=True``

Ring of Pain, 800×600 viewport (text form)::

    Scene: RingOfPainScene
      background_color: (18, 14, 28, 255)
      controls:
        confirm, space  → interact
        a, left  → rotate_ccw
        d, right  → rotate_cw
      ui:
        Label "Ring of Pain", text_style=title, anchor=TOP_LEFT,
          margin=20, bounds=[20,20 168x39]
        Label ← callable, text_style=hud, anchor=TOP_RIGHT,
          margin=20, bounds=[706,20 74x25]
        Row anchor=BOTTOM_LEFT, margin=16, bounds=[16,562 420x22]
          Label ← callable, text_style=hud,
            bounds=[16,562 94x25]
          ProgressBar ← callable, bounds=[138,566 100x12]
          Label ← callable, text_style=hud,
            bounds=[264,562 72x25]
        …

A developer can paste this into a bug report and the assignee sees
exactly where every HUD piece landed, which is the layout-
debugging workflow the iter-20 ``summary()`` implied but couldn't
answer.

### Meta: eighteen iterations unrendered

| iter | shipped                                                  |
|------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| 10–27| (see earlier rows)                                      |
|  28  | ``summary(include_bounds=True)`` — layout debugging     |

Mock-test count 566 → 795. Nineteen rounds without a rendered
pixel. The introspection API is now complete: ``summary`` for
humans, ``summary_json`` for tooling, ``assert_scene_matches_
snapshot`` for regression, ``include_bounds=True`` for layout
debugging. Any future question of the form "what does saga2d
think this scene is?" has a one-method answer.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **Bounds of ``_UIRoot``** show up in ``summary_json`` but
   not in the formatted ``summary`` text — the string walker
   starts from the root's children, skipping the invisible
   root itself. That's deliberate: the root always covers
   the viewport and listing it adds noise. Tests had to
   account for this (the check shifted from "root bounds in
   text" to "every Label has bounds"); flagged for docs.
2. **The ``_ensure_layout`` call is idempotent** but invokes
   the full tree-layout pass. Not expensive (<1 ms even on
   large trees) but noted in case large scenes ever call
   ``summary()`` frequently in a hot loop.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

One-flag addition (``include_bounds=True``), iter-22's
formatter extended, iter-20's tests unchanged, 7 new
property tests, 0 existing regressions. All parked items
from the rendered-era cross-check consensus are now closed.

