## Iteration 36 — 2026-04-17

Closed the bug the iter-35 diagnostic warning surfaced. Clean
closure of a surprising find — my own warning change was the
mechanism that revealed a pre-existing issue, and this round fixed
it.

### What shipped

* **``examples/battle_vignette/battle_unit.py``** and
  **``examples/battle_vignette/battle_demo.py``** —
  ``play_sound("sounds/X")`` corrected to ``play_sound("X")`` on
  all eight call sites. The prefix was redundant: saga2d's
  ``AssetManager.sound(name)`` resolves to
  ``<base_path>/sounds/{name}.wav`` automatically, so passing
  ``"sounds/X"`` made the resolver look for
  ``<base_path>/sounds/sounds/X.wav`` which didn't exist. The
  ``optional=True`` flag meant this failed silently before
  iter-35 and with a warning afterwards — but the sounds never
  actually played for the battle example, despite existing in
  its ``assets/sounds/`` directory.

833 mock-backend tests pass — and the warning count dropped
from 20 (iter-35) to zero (this round). Clean bill of health.

### Meta: the diagnostic loop closed in one round

iter-30 added an ``AssetManager`` font warning for silent
fallbacks. iter-35 added the audio equivalent, as a parallel
improvement. The audio warning immediately surfaced
twenty silently-failing calls in a pre-existing example —
exactly the "silent failure makes 'why is there no sound' hard
to diagnose" concern the warning was added for.

iter-36 fixed the surfaced issue.

This is the diagnostic loop working as intended: add a
warning → run the tests → observe what fires → fix the surfaced
bug. Saga2d's own improvement paid for itself on the very next
iteration, on code that had been silently broken for an unknown
amount of time before this run started.

