## Iteration 40 — 2026-04-16

Shipped a new :class:`CircularGauge` widget and used it to
replace Ring of Pain's rectangular HP bar. This addresses
iter-38/39's "HUD stylistic-clash" consensus finding with a
general-purpose reusable component rather than a one-off fix.
Closed the diagnostic loop end-to-end a second time: consensus
issue surfaced in iter-38 → investigated in iter-39 (typography
& layout) → widget-level fix in iter-40 → re-cross-check
confirms the finding moved out of consensus.

### What shipped

* **``saga2d.CircularGauge`**. 200 LOC widget in
  ``saga2d/ui/widgets.py``. Same reactive contract as
  :class:`ProgressBar` (``value=callable``, ``max_value=callable``,
  refreshed each frame). Renders as a disc slot with an inner
  fill disc sized by the fraction. Optional rim colour for the
  rim-and-fill style used by Ring of Pain nodes. Added to
  public exports on both ``saga2d`` and ``saga2d.ui``.
* **Ring of Pain HUD restyle**. Previous HUD row was
  ``Label("HP") + ProgressBar(rectangular pink pill) +
  Label("Coins")``. iter-40 swaps the ProgressBar for a
  ``CircularGauge(radius=11, fill=HP_COLOR, rim=...)``. The HUD
  now visually belongs to the same family as the ring of
  circular nodes above — one visual language instead of two.
* **Ten CircularGauge property tests** (``tests/ui/
  test_circular_gauge.py``). Half are shared-contract with
  ProgressBar (fraction arithmetic, NaN guards, reactive
  rebinding). The other half verify *visual* properties via
  the iter-38 mock-to-PIL renderer — the centre pixel of a
  full gauge is the fill colour, the centre pixel of an empty
  gauge is the empty colour, a half-full gauge's 15-px-out
  pixel is empty-colour. These rely on ``draw_circle``
  predictability and pass deterministically.

860 mock-backend tests pass (10 new; previously 850).

### The diagnostic loop ran cleanly a second time

| iter | cross-check consensus on Ring of Pain render           |
|------|-------------------------------------------------------|
|  38  | 4 font sizes · **pink bar clashes** · bottom collision |
|  39  | 4 sizes → 3 · pink bar clashes · node text too small   |
|  40  | HUD lacks grounding · node label spacing · type hier.  |

iter-38's "bottom collision" → drift in iter-39 (fixed by
``margin_bottom`` bump).  iter-38's "4 font sizes" → drift in
iter-40 (fixed by iter-39's ``sub`` / ``caption`` unification).
iter-38/39's "pink HP bar clashes with circular aesthetic" →
**gone entirely in iter-40** (CircularGauge replaced it). The
cross-check synthesis no longer mentions the bar at all.

The new consensus point is narrower: "HUD needs a containing
panel to feel grounded." That's a more mundane UX improvement,
not a stylistic clash. Progress.

### Meta: 40 iterations, 2 diagnostic loops closed

The iter-7/8 cross-check methodology was aimed at exactly this
pattern: real cross-model consensus → fix → re-cross-check →
issue either dissolves or crystallises. Before iter-38 there
was no rendering pipeline for the loop to run on. In iter-38
the pipeline came online. In iter-39 and iter-40 the loop ran
twice and closed cleanly each time — iter-39 on a layout bug,
iter-40 on an aesthetic widget-level fix.

Mock-backend test count 850 → 860. CircularGauge is
zero-external-dependency (same draw_circle primitive as every
other saga2d circle) and self-contained — the only new code is
one file with tests.

### Keras-for-game-dev dimension this iteration

Keras ships prebuilt layers (``Conv2D``, ``Dropout``,
``BatchNormalization``). saga2d ships prebuilt widgets. Before
iter-40: ``Label``, ``Button``, ``Panel``, ``Row``, ``Column``,
``ProgressBar``, ``TextBox``, ``List``, ``Grid``, ``Tooltip``,
``TabGroup``, ``DataTable``, ``ImageBox``. iter-40 adds
``CircularGauge`` — a disc counterpart to ProgressBar for games
with circular art, filling out the widget vocabulary one bit
more. The pattern is "pick a widget, pass a reactive callable,
the framework handles drawing and updating" — identical to
Keras's "pick a layer, pass a shape, the framework handles
gradients and weights."

Where saga2d still diverges from Keras is in the *introspection
story*. Keras's ``model.summary()`` reads cleanly because each
layer's shape is mechanically derivable from its predecessor.
saga2d's ``Scene.summary()`` (iter-24) lists the UI tree but
not the visual footprint (how much screen real estate does this
HUD row claim? which widgets overlap which?). A future
iteration could add ``Scene.summary(include_bounds=True)`` to
surface *visual* structure the same way Keras surfaces *tensor*
structure.

### API friction noticed this iteration

1. **CircularGauge shares a lot with ProgressBar**. Both have
   ``value``, ``max_value``, ``_refresh``, ``fraction``. Both
   validate finiteness. Copy-paste rather than abstract base
   felt right for two instances — if a third gauge-like widget
   appears (RadialArc? Pie?) a ``ReactiveRatioWidget`` mixin
   would be worth extracting. Three similar lines is better
   than a premature abstraction.
2. **The rim-color rendering uses 4 draw_circle calls to
   simulate a ring**. A first-class ``draw_ring(cx, cy, r,
   ring_width, color)`` primitive on the backend would cut
   this to 1 call and be sharper on a GPU backend. Parked —
   not worth adding until a second user appears.
3. **GPT-5.1 called the new gauge "the HP pill icon is
   squashed"**. The gauge is ``radius=11``, diameter 22 px,
   rendered next to an 18-pt text label. At this scale, PIL
   draws it slightly stippled. Bumping to ``radius=13``
   would read more solidly — considered for iter-41.

### Concrete steps taken this iteration

One widget, ten property tests, one HUD restyle in Ring of
Pain, one cross-check. The consensus point that has been open
since iter-38 is now closed. No pyglet in sight still.

### Parked for iteration 41

* **HUD grounding** — iter-40's cross-check consensus. A
  subtle semi-transparent panel behind the HUD row would
  address the "disconnected / floating" feedback. Fits the
  circular aesthetic if the panel is an oval or rounded
  container (or simply a darker background rectangle with
  low opacity).
* **CircularGauge radius bump** — iter-40's drift (GPT only):
  ``radius=11`` → ``radius=13`` would read cleaner at the
  HUD scale. Not a consensus issue yet; deferred.
* **Scene.summary(include_bounds=True)** — visual footprint
  introspection. The Keras-parallel step.
* **Pyglet render** — still blocked.
* **Second user** — still outstanding.

