### API friction noticed this iteration

(Friction also listed in the "surfaced, not yet fixed"
section above — ``is_pressed`` and AABB helpers were the
pain points.)

4. **``backend.images`` vs ``backend.sprites`` is a confusing
   split**. Images are per-frame blits (cleared every tick);
   sprites are persistent state the scene manages. A new
   user writing either a scene with ``draw_image`` calls or
   a scene with Sprite instances sees different recording
   paths in the mock backend when debugging. A unified
   ``backend.get_frame_draw_ops()`` that returns both kinds
   with consistent metadata would simplify assertions.
5. **``Sprite.position`` is a ``tuple[float, float]`` but
   ``Sprite.x`` / ``Sprite.y`` are float properties set
   independently**. Makes sense individually but led to a
   confusion where I nearly did ``sprite.position = (x,
   sprite.position[1])`` instead of ``sprite.x = x``. A
   ``sprite.set_position(x=…, y=…)`` convenience would be
   kinder.

